{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Resuming an interrupted evaluation that includes a retired model is refused, preventing supported work from continuing."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A bare IPv6 SSH destination causes remote-management actions to fail before contacting the host."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Using an SSH alias with an IP-based provider URL can produce a false unhealthy result and leave provider enablement unchanged."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Previously saved routing settings that name a retired model or provider can prevent the daemon from starting after upgrade."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"normal","reason":"The documentation link lands on a different provider section, leaving the reader to find the example."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An operator following the inconsistent binary-path documentation can generate a unit that fails to start the remote server."},{"id":"C1b","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A retired model in a saved fallback chain causes resume to be refused even when supported targets remain."}]}